WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:03.080
No TV show is perfect — not even Game of
Thrones.

00:00:03.140 --> 00:00:07.540
While the fantasy drama series has garnered
a reputation for its attention to detail,

00:00:07.540 --> 00:00:11.910
the people in charge got a little lazy on
the latest episode, with fans spotting a glaring

00:00:11.910 --> 00:00:13.540
mistake sitting in plain sight.

00:00:13.560 --> 00:00:17.360
If you haven't seen the episode yourself,
watch out — there are spoilers incoming.

00:00:17.560 --> 00:00:21.760
Entitled "The Last of the Starks," episode
4 of Game of Thrones season 8 would have been

00:00:21.770 --> 00:00:25.949
more appropriately named "The First of the
Starbucks," as a single paper coffee cup was

00:00:25.949 --> 00:00:29.360
accidentally left on a table while shooting
— and it made the final edit.

00:00:29.460 --> 00:00:30.900
"How could you let this happen?"

00:00:31.190 --> 00:00:35.460
The immersion-destroying cup can be seen just
next to Daenerys Targaryen in the Great Hall

00:00:35.460 --> 00:00:39.050
at Winterfell's castle, where the survivors
of the Battle of Winterfell are celebrating

00:00:39.050 --> 00:00:41.640
victory over the Night King and the Army of
the Dead.

00:00:41.820 --> 00:00:45.680
Jon Snow is laughing it up with his pals;
Brienne, Podrick, and the Lannister brothers

00:00:45.690 --> 00:00:50.050
are playing a drinking game, Sansa is chatting
with the Hound; and Daenerys is quietly freaking

00:00:50.050 --> 00:00:54.629
out over how well-liked Jon is, knowing that
if word of his true parentage gets out, almost

00:00:54.629 --> 00:00:57.340
everyone will side with him over her to take
the Iron Throne.

00:00:57.360 --> 00:01:01.579
As Tormund sings Jon's praises while Dany
watches, just between them on the table is

00:01:01.580 --> 00:01:05.260
that out-of-place, out-of-time coffee cup,
with a sleeve and a lid and everything.

00:01:05.260 --> 00:01:07.440
The only thing we don't see is an actor's
name.

00:01:07.590 --> 00:01:11.620
Game of Thrones fans were quick to spot the
error and post about it on social media, and

00:01:11.630 --> 00:01:15.180
though some initially believed that the photos
they saw online were fake, a rewatch of the

00:01:15.180 --> 00:01:19.150
scene proves that it's no farce — the most
recent episode of Game of Thrones really did

00:01:19.150 --> 00:01:23.180
make a mistake by not clearing the table and
accidentally including a coffee cup in the

00:01:23.180 --> 00:01:23.680
shot.

00:01:23.880 --> 00:01:24.760
"Madness.

00:01:24.980 --> 00:01:27.140
Madness and stupidity."

00:01:27.330 --> 00:01:31.100
Plenty of viewers found the blunder funny,
while others took a harsher stance and slammed

00:01:31.110 --> 00:01:34.490
the Game of Thrones creative team for being
oblivious to the slip-up.

00:01:34.490 --> 00:01:36.000
Journalist Eric Seales tweeted:

00:01:36.040 --> 00:01:40.400
"So it takes @HBO @GameOfThrones almost 2
years to shoot season 8 and they forgot to

00:01:40.400 --> 00:01:43.820
take away #Daenerys #Targaryen's @Starbucks
cup in yesterday's episode??

00:01:44.040 --> 00:01:44.740
Oops! #starbuckscup"

00:01:44.960 --> 00:01:47.800
The folks from the You Watch, I Listen podcast
had this to add:

00:01:48.020 --> 00:01:52.460
"Seriously how did the Game of Thrones directors
and editors absolutely MISS a Starbucks cup

00:01:52.470 --> 00:01:54.280
left on the table during that scene?

00:01:54.280 --> 00:01:55.140
'He's Jon Snow.

00:01:55.140 --> 00:01:55.880
King in the North.

00:01:56.020 --> 00:01:57.100
The drinker of latte's.'"

00:01:57.160 --> 00:02:00.920
Many commenters felt it was pretty incredible
that despite years of work and millions of

00:02:00.920 --> 00:02:05.130
dollars spent to complete season 8's six episodes,
everyone behind the scenes from the set to

00:02:05.130 --> 00:02:07.920
the editing bay just missed the presence of
the wayward coffee cup.

00:02:08.140 --> 00:02:12.100
What I Like About Me author Jenna Guillaume
even called back to episode 3's technical

00:02:12.100 --> 00:02:13.220
problems by joking,

00:02:13.440 --> 00:02:17.080
"maybe if they lit the show better they'd
be able to spot their own basic mistakes."

00:02:17.090 --> 00:02:20.370
The quips kept coming as the night continued,
with one fan writing,

00:02:20.370 --> 00:02:23.940
"feeling sorry for the starbucks [barista]
that had to write out 'Daenerys Stormborn

00:02:23.940 --> 00:02:27.970
of the House Targaryen, First of Her Name,
the Unburnt, Queen of the Andals and the First

00:02:27.970 --> 00:02:32.120
Men, Khaleesi of the Great Grass Sea, Breaker
of Chains, and Mother of Dragons.'"

00:02:32.260 --> 00:02:33.100
What a mouthful!

00:02:33.500 --> 00:02:37.640
Though the immersion-breaking coffee cup seen
in the episode sure looks like one from Starbucks,

00:02:37.640 --> 00:02:38.380
it apparently isn't.

00:02:38.640 --> 00:02:42.160
According to Game of Thrones art director
Hauke Richter, it's actually from a local

00:02:42.160 --> 00:02:45.980
coffeehouse in the town of Banbridge, Northern
Ireland, around where the series filmed that

00:02:45.980 --> 00:02:46.980
particular episode.

00:02:46.980 --> 00:02:51.120
Richter, who has worked on Game of Thrones
for the last five years, also told TMZ that

00:02:51.120 --> 00:02:54.270
the coffee cup was an unfortunate mistake,
and likely exhaustion-related.

00:02:54.270 --> 00:02:55.260
He said,

00:02:55.380 --> 00:02:57.820
"We are usually so diligent that this does
not happen.

00:02:58.000 --> 00:03:01.980
The shoot was very hard and demanding and
it is likely that after a very tiring [episode]

00:03:01.980 --> 00:03:05.220
3 shoot, this was simply overlooked by an
exhausted crew."

00:03:05.220 --> 00:03:09.140
The art director added that errors like this
happen quite often on television and movies,

00:03:09.140 --> 00:03:13.140
but that he felt people were quicker to notice
this particular mistake due to Game of Thrones'

00:03:13.140 --> 00:03:13.640
popularity.

00:03:13.800 --> 00:03:17.940
As for HBO, the network released a statement
the following day which helped to explain

00:03:17.950 --> 00:03:19.110
things, reading in part,

00:03:19.110 --> 00:03:21.220
"The latte that appeared in the episode was
a mistake.

00:03:21.270 --> 00:03:22.900
Daenerys had ordered an herbal tea."

00:03:23.540 --> 00:03:26.980
Though the coffee cup seen on "The Last of
the Starks" may have been a big blunder, it's

00:03:26.980 --> 00:03:28.200
ultimately a harmless one.

00:03:28.520 --> 00:03:32.740
In fact, if you load up the episode on HBO's
streaming services now, you won't find it.

00:03:32.740 --> 00:03:37.140
Just a few days after the episode aired, HBO
announced that the editing wizards had digitally

00:03:37.150 --> 00:03:39.760
removed the cup from the feasting table in
Winterfell.

00:03:39.840 --> 00:03:43.900
While the errant cup will live on in internet
infamy forever, no longer shall a crew member's

00:03:43.900 --> 00:03:47.140
leftover beverage sully your Game of Thrones
viewing experience.

00:03:47.140 --> 00:03:48.540
Praise to the seven.

00:03:48.620 --> 00:03:50.140
"Bloody ridiculous."

